1
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:13,918
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:17,004
Ah, summer's here again

3
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:19,924
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,010
Ah, summer's here again

5
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,596
It's come, it's arrived, here it is!

6
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,850
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,477
Here they come on the southern wind

8
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,730
Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs

9
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:37,733
At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!

10
00:00:37,942 --> 00:00:40,736
Ah, summer's here again

11
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:43,781
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,576
Ah, summer's here again

13
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:49,245
It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!

14
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:52,498
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

15
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:55,334
Here they come on the southern wind

16
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:58,337
Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts

17
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:02,842
At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:15,313
Here they come on the southern wind

19
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:21,861
Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach

20
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:24,280
Want you!

21
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:33,998
OPEN THE KACHIDOKI BRIDGE!

22
00:01:40,296 --> 00:01:43,257
-It was a lovely wedding. -Yeah.

23
00:01:43,466 --> 00:01:44,717
Cheers!

24
00:01:49,263 --> 00:01:53,434
Hey, as we're in Ginza, let's go see the Kachidoki Bridge before we head back.

25
00:01:53,643 --> 00:01:54,936
But that's the opposite direction.

26
00:01:55,144 --> 00:01:56,812
What? If you complain, I'll do this...

27
00:01:57,021 --> 00:01:59,023
Argh! Okay, okay!

28
00:01:59,232 --> 00:02:00,441
Good.

29
00:02:02,985 --> 00:02:04,695
Jeez, Ryo-chan.

30
00:02:15,665 --> 00:02:17,458
Ryo-chan, we're on the Kachidoki Bridge.

31
00:02:19,126 --> 00:02:21,170
We've arrived, Ryo-chan. Wake up!

32
00:02:21,587 --> 00:02:24,215
Come on, it was you who wanted to come...

33
00:02:24,423 --> 00:02:25,299
Oh!

34
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,637
-Stop the car! -Huh?

35
00:02:34,684 --> 00:02:35,851
What happened?

36
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,855
-I saw a man on the bridge. -What?

37
00:02:39,188 --> 00:02:40,898
Probably just a ghost.

38
00:02:48,030 --> 00:02:49,740
Where was he, Reiko?

39
00:02:49,949 --> 00:02:51,951
Over here, on this steel frame.

40
00:02:55,371 --> 00:02:56,747
Are you sure?

41
00:02:56,956 --> 00:03:00,918
Yes, I did see him. He looked like he was about to jump.

42
00:03:01,127 --> 00:03:02,128
Oh no!

43
00:03:09,135 --> 00:03:12,430
That was such a great wedding.

44
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,600
And I saw a lucky tea stalk in my tea this morning.

45
00:03:15,808 --> 00:03:17,768
So, I'm in a great mood.

46
00:03:19,395 --> 00:03:22,940
Yes, I see. Thank you very much for your time.

47
00:03:23,983 --> 00:03:28,237
It seems there were no incidents or accidents near the Kachidoki Bridge.

48
00:03:28,779 --> 00:03:31,741
The Kachidoki Bridge?

49
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:34,285
But I wonder why that man was there...

50
00:03:34,493 --> 00:03:36,203
Good morning, everyone.

51
00:03:41,334 --> 00:03:45,463
You're lucky, Ryotsu. The chief is in a really good mood this morning.

52
00:03:45,713 --> 00:03:46,672
Lucky me!

53
00:03:47,298 --> 00:03:49,508
Good morning, sir.

54
00:03:49,717 --> 00:03:50,968
I drank a bit too much...

55
00:03:51,177 --> 00:03:54,388
You idiot! What time do you call this?

56
00:03:54,597 --> 00:03:56,891
Argh, don't yell at me.

57
00:03:57,099 --> 00:03:58,643
It's ringing in my head.

58
00:03:59,644 --> 00:04:02,897
-I'll make your head really ring! -Don't drag me like a stray cat!

59
00:04:03,648 --> 00:04:05,858
Hey, how can you say he's in a good mood?

60
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:07,401
Come here right now!

61
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:12,531
What happened? He was in such a good mood.

62
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,408
You moron!

63
00:04:20,414 --> 00:04:21,457
Illegal parking.

64
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:22,833
Good morning.

65
00:04:23,042 --> 00:04:25,002
Oh, it's a Sapporo plate.

66
00:04:25,211 --> 00:04:29,590
Yes. It's been illegally parked near the Kachidoki Bridge.

67
00:04:30,091 --> 00:04:32,259
-The Kachidoki Bridge? -Right.

68
00:04:32,468 --> 00:04:37,348
A neighbor said they saw a tall man in white clothes get out.

69
00:04:37,556 --> 00:04:40,601
White clothes? It could be the guy from last night.

70
00:04:41,394 --> 00:04:44,605
Hello. Could you check the owner of this car?

71
00:04:44,814 --> 00:04:46,023
It's a Sapporo plate.

72
00:04:46,232 --> 00:04:49,026
Looks like it's not just a parking violation.

73
00:04:49,694 --> 00:04:50,653
Is it an incident?

74
00:04:50,861 --> 00:04:54,615
Well, it's not confirmed yet that it's the car of the man from last night.

75
00:04:55,032 --> 00:04:58,369
Got it. Toyohira Ward, Sapporo City.

76
00:04:58,828 --> 00:05:02,832
Owner is Jun Shiratori, written with the characters for "purity" and "white bird."

77
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,208
Thank you.

78
00:05:04,417 --> 00:05:06,335
What's wrong with Jun Shiratori?

79
00:05:07,253 --> 00:05:08,295
Oww, my head.

80
00:05:08,504 --> 00:05:09,755
Do you know him, Ryo-chan?

81
00:05:09,964 --> 00:05:10,881
Yeah.

82
00:05:11,882 --> 00:05:14,093
He's a friend from junior high school,

83
00:05:14,301 --> 00:05:16,846
although he wasn't there for long.

84
00:05:17,346 --> 00:05:21,851
He left his car near the Kachidoki Bridge and then disappeared.

85
00:05:22,351 --> 00:05:25,855
The Kachidoki Bridge? Oh, he must've come to see it!

86
00:05:26,355 --> 00:05:27,189
The bridge?

87
00:05:27,398 --> 00:05:29,358
What do you mean, Ryotsu?

88
00:05:29,734 --> 00:05:34,280
Well, it all happened when I was an adorable junior high school student...

89
00:05:34,488 --> 00:05:35,448
Kankichi Ryotsu.

90
00:05:35,656 --> 00:05:36,615
Yes.

91
00:05:44,457 --> 00:05:45,958
Wow!

92
00:05:46,167 --> 00:05:48,627
Super spinning somersault!

93
00:05:50,755 --> 00:05:51,756
I feel dizzy!

94
00:05:57,595 --> 00:05:58,429
Ouch...

95
00:05:59,472 --> 00:06:02,933
Kankichi! Who told you to spin in the air!

96
00:06:03,142 --> 00:06:03,976
Just a little bonus.

97
00:06:08,022 --> 00:06:10,191
Kan-chan, you're great!

98
00:06:11,317 --> 00:06:12,943
Jun, did you enjoy that?

99
00:06:13,152 --> 00:06:15,654
Next time, I'll show you a more spectacular one.

100
00:06:15,863 --> 00:06:16,989
Kankichi!

101
00:06:17,198 --> 00:06:18,032
Yes!

102
00:06:23,287 --> 00:06:27,082
Wow, you went to the World Expo, Jun-kun? That's awesome!

103
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:30,336
But it was so crowded that I couldn't see much of it.

104
00:06:30,544 --> 00:06:33,672
He got the bullet train there. Tonkichi, have you ever ridden it?

105
00:06:33,923 --> 00:06:35,758
I've only ridden the Tobu Line.

106
00:06:37,384 --> 00:06:38,469
Would you like some tea?

107
00:06:38,886 --> 00:06:40,763
Sorry to bother you.

108
00:06:42,056 --> 00:06:43,474
Help yourself, boys.

109
00:06:43,682 --> 00:06:45,768
Oh, cakes again!

110
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:48,104
You're always so kind, Mrs. Shiratori.

111
00:06:48,437 --> 00:06:50,898
It's okay. Please continue to get along with Jun.

112
00:06:51,315 --> 00:06:52,191
Sure!

113
00:06:52,399 --> 00:06:54,276
Make yourself at home, then.

114
00:06:56,403 --> 00:07:00,407
Even when I can't take part in gym class, I never get bored watching you guys.

115
00:07:00,866 --> 00:07:03,869
Kankichi's only talent is his energy after all.

116
00:07:05,412 --> 00:07:06,413
-Hey! -Ouch!

117
00:07:07,039 --> 00:07:08,541
Next time, I'll do a backflip.

118
00:07:08,749 --> 00:07:11,627
In return, show me your answers again on the next test.

119
00:07:11,836 --> 00:07:14,922
My eyesight is 20/8, perfect for cheating on tests!

120
00:07:20,636 --> 00:07:23,180
By the way, you have so many books.

121
00:07:23,389 --> 00:07:24,974
Have you read them all?

122
00:07:25,182 --> 00:07:27,768
Almost. I'll lend one to you anytime.

123
00:07:28,477 --> 00:07:32,231
We're not good with thick books like these. Right, Tonkichi?

124
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:34,775
Yeah, textbooks are more than enough.

125
00:07:35,526 --> 00:07:39,029
Oh! I think this one is interesting.

126
00:07:42,616 --> 00:07:44,952
"Japanese..." Um...

127
00:07:45,161 --> 00:07:46,954
"Japanese Movable Bridges."

128
00:07:47,329 --> 00:07:50,291
So this is the kind of thing you like.

129
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,628
Oh, this is the Kachidoki Bridge!

130
00:07:55,045 --> 00:07:57,756
-That's right. -Yeah, it is.

131
00:07:57,965 --> 00:07:58,883
Do you know it?

132
00:07:59,341 --> 00:08:01,886
Ha, I know a bit about bridges.

133
00:08:02,094 --> 00:08:05,306
Shirahige, Kototoi, Azuma, Komagata, Umaya,

134
00:08:05,514 --> 00:08:09,351
Kuramae, Ryogoku, Kiyosu, Eitai, Tsukuda, and Kachidoki.

135
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:12,313
Those are all the bridges on the Sumida River.

136
00:08:12,521 --> 00:08:13,439
Wow!

137
00:08:13,647 --> 00:08:16,358
We had to remember them in elementary school.

138
00:08:17,109 --> 00:08:19,528
My favorite is the Kachidoki Bridge,

139
00:08:19,737 --> 00:08:22,031
'cause it moves with a loud noise.

140
00:08:22,865 --> 00:08:25,075
Oh, I wish I could see it someday.

141
00:08:25,576 --> 00:08:27,369
Huh? You've never seen it?

142
00:08:27,578 --> 00:08:30,372
I want to see it, but it's so far away.

143
00:08:32,124 --> 00:08:34,543
It's not that far, just beyond Ginza.

144
00:08:34,752 --> 00:08:39,340
All the cars stop, and the bridge opens slowly like this.

145
00:08:39,965 --> 00:08:43,135
When you watch from the edge, the road comes at you like a wall.

146
00:08:43,344 --> 00:08:45,429
It's so impressive.

147
00:08:46,805 --> 00:08:49,308
That's amazing! I'd love to see it with my own eyes.

148
00:08:49,516 --> 00:08:51,644
Why don't we go to see it now?

149
00:08:51,852 --> 00:08:53,771
It's about 20 minutes by bike.

150
00:08:55,105 --> 00:08:56,023
Okay!

151
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,945
All right. Let's go!

152
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:16,210
Then, a hero of justice appeared! Ta-da!

153
00:09:28,097 --> 00:09:29,848
We're almost there.

154
00:09:36,689 --> 00:09:37,523
Look, there it is.

155
00:09:38,607 --> 00:09:40,067
Wow!

156
00:09:40,609 --> 00:09:42,653
You'd never guess it opens.

157
00:09:45,197 --> 00:09:47,324
The view from here is perfect.

158
00:09:47,533 --> 00:09:50,494
I always buy bread and watch it while eating.

159
00:09:50,703 --> 00:09:52,204
Oh, here comes a boat.

160
00:09:52,788 --> 00:09:54,832
Great! It's going to open.

161
00:09:57,084 --> 00:10:00,170
Here it goes, up, up!

162
00:10:01,130 --> 00:10:02,131
Huh?

163
00:10:04,174 --> 00:10:05,467
It's not opening.

164
00:10:05,676 --> 00:10:09,054
That's strange. It usually opens around now.

165
00:10:09,263 --> 00:10:10,848
I wonder what's going on.

166
00:10:17,229 --> 00:10:18,856
What? It doesn't open anymore?

167
00:10:19,064 --> 00:10:20,941
Yesterday was the last time.

168
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:24,028
They say movable bridges are out of fashion now.

169
00:10:24,987 --> 00:10:27,573
We've entered the era of land transportation.

170
00:10:27,781 --> 00:10:30,075
Even though transporting by water is easier.

171
00:10:30,659 --> 00:10:32,328
I had no idea.

172
00:10:32,536 --> 00:10:33,370
Darn it!

173
00:10:33,579 --> 00:10:35,581
The Kachidoki Bridge won't open anymore?

174
00:10:35,789 --> 00:10:39,585
It's a government decision, so I doubt it.

175
00:10:40,169 --> 00:10:45,215
It's always weak people like us who suffer when the times change.

176
00:10:57,353 --> 00:11:00,689
Dang, we came all the way to see it. What a bummer!

177
00:11:02,691 --> 00:11:05,402
Jun-kun was really looking forward to it, too.

178
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,529
Don't feel down, Jun.

179
00:11:09,114 --> 00:11:10,157
Yeah.

180
00:11:14,495 --> 00:11:15,370
Kondo.

181
00:11:15,579 --> 00:11:16,580
Here!

182
00:11:16,789 --> 00:11:17,748
Shibayama.

183
00:11:17,956 --> 00:11:18,791
Here!

184
00:11:18,999 --> 00:11:22,086
Shiratori is absent.

185
00:11:23,253 --> 00:11:25,589
Sir! What happened to Jun?

186
00:11:26,131 --> 00:11:28,592
I heard he's got a fever and is resting in bed.

187
00:11:29,301 --> 00:11:33,597
He was pretty shocked by what happened with the bridge.

188
00:11:33,806 --> 00:11:35,265
Let's go see him after school.

189
00:11:36,266 --> 00:11:37,768
You're changing schools?

190
00:11:38,310 --> 00:11:41,438
I'm moving to Hokkaido, where the air is fresher.

191
00:11:41,647 --> 00:11:44,399
Just when I'd made friends with you guys...

192
00:11:47,444 --> 00:11:49,780
Even if you go far away, we'll still be friends.

193
00:11:49,988 --> 00:11:51,448
-Right? -Sure.

194
00:11:51,657 --> 00:11:56,537
Yes, of course. But there's just one thing I regret.

195
00:11:56,745 --> 00:11:59,581
I couldn't see the Kachidoki Bridge open.

196
00:12:00,290 --> 00:12:02,668
I wish we could've seen it together.

197
00:12:02,876 --> 00:12:05,421
Jun, when are you going to Hokkaido?

198
00:12:06,255 --> 00:12:07,089
In two days.

199
00:12:07,714 --> 00:12:09,383
That soon?

200
00:12:15,305 --> 00:12:18,642
So Jun-kun's moving away. That's too bad.

201
00:12:18,851 --> 00:12:21,854
I'll never get to eat such delicious cake again in my life.

202
00:12:22,479 --> 00:12:25,482
Kankichi's test scores will be back to zero again.

203
00:12:34,533 --> 00:12:38,287
Jun-kun was really disappointed about the bridge.

204
00:12:38,745 --> 00:12:41,498
I wanted him to see it opening.

205
00:12:42,374 --> 00:12:43,292
I've got it!

206
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:46,628
Let's show him the bridge opening!

207
00:12:46,837 --> 00:12:47,671
Huh?

208
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,215
But, it's impossible now.

209
00:12:50,924 --> 00:12:56,096
We'll open it ourselves. Open the bridge and show it to Jun!

210
00:12:56,305 --> 00:12:57,347
What?

211
00:13:13,947 --> 00:13:15,240
Kan-chan!

212
00:13:19,328 --> 00:13:20,245
Yo!

213
00:13:22,206 --> 00:13:24,082
What's up? Why are you up here?

214
00:13:24,583 --> 00:13:27,544
Come with me! I'll show you the Kachidoki Bridge opening!

215
00:13:27,753 --> 00:13:29,838
What? Is the bridge going to open?

216
00:13:30,047 --> 00:13:31,965
Yes! So, hurry up!

217
00:13:32,174 --> 00:13:34,384
Just wait here. I'll change my clothes.

218
00:13:38,555 --> 00:13:39,723
This way!

219
00:13:42,267 --> 00:13:44,686
Shh! I'll be right back, John.

220
00:13:55,197 --> 00:13:58,075
This is definitely the best place to see the bridge.

221
00:13:58,283 --> 00:13:59,743
Jun-kun, you just wait here.

222
00:14:00,786 --> 00:14:02,537
Will the bridge really open?

223
00:14:03,288 --> 00:14:05,541
Don't worry. Leave it to us.

224
00:14:05,749 --> 00:14:07,542
-Okay, let's go! -All right.

225
00:14:18,637 --> 00:14:21,807
The Kachidoki Bridge has four towers.

226
00:14:24,309 --> 00:14:29,731
Only that one has a staircase. The control room must be in there.

227
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:33,110
I'll open the bridge. You two, stop the cars.

228
00:14:33,318 --> 00:14:34,152
All right!

229
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,161
Sure enough, there it is.

230
00:14:45,414 --> 00:14:47,124
Of course, the door is locked.

231
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,126
But that won't stop me.

232
00:14:51,003 --> 00:14:52,629
I'm pretty good at opening doors.

233
00:14:53,213 --> 00:14:54,631
Stop!

234
00:14:55,090 --> 00:14:56,091
Please stop!

235
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:58,093
The bridge is going to open!

236
00:15:01,722 --> 00:15:03,849
It's no use! They won't stop.

237
00:15:04,057 --> 00:15:05,726
Not on this side, either.

238
00:15:07,728 --> 00:15:08,645
It's open!

239
00:15:09,396 --> 00:15:10,230
A piece of cake!

240
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:18,488
So many switches.

241
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,704
I guess it won't work unless I turn it on.

242
00:15:25,912 --> 00:15:27,664
How does it work?

243
00:15:28,081 --> 00:15:29,499
Stop your cars!

244
00:15:29,708 --> 00:15:30,834
Please!

245
00:15:31,043 --> 00:15:31,877
Stop!

246
00:15:32,085 --> 00:15:33,503
The bridge is opening!

247
00:15:33,712 --> 00:15:35,047
Damn it!

248
00:15:35,255 --> 00:15:36,673
Stop!

249
00:15:38,884 --> 00:15:40,927
Yes! It stopped!

250
00:15:46,224 --> 00:15:48,393
What are you boys doing?

251
00:15:49,436 --> 00:15:51,938
Why are you stopping cars?

252
00:15:53,565 --> 00:15:54,524
Hey!

253
00:15:58,695 --> 00:16:00,864
Kankichi, the cops found us!

254
00:16:02,616 --> 00:16:04,368
Hey! Stop!

255
00:16:15,379 --> 00:16:17,005
Tonkichi, close the door!

256
00:16:20,842 --> 00:16:22,219
Hey! Open it!

257
00:16:22,427 --> 00:16:23,470
What are you up to?

258
00:16:23,845 --> 00:16:27,391
It's over! The cars won't stop and the cops found us!

259
00:16:27,599 --> 00:16:29,976
Our plan was too reckless. Let's call it off!

260
00:16:30,727 --> 00:16:33,105
Idiot! Jun is waiting for us!

261
00:16:34,523 --> 00:16:36,483
Will it really open?

262
00:16:38,068 --> 00:16:41,238
But how can you open the bridge in the first place?

263
00:16:41,446 --> 00:16:43,073
Let's give up!

264
00:16:44,324 --> 00:16:45,409
Hey! Open the door!

265
00:16:45,617 --> 00:16:46,993
Get out of there now!

266
00:16:47,494 --> 00:16:49,204
What should we do, Kankichi?

267
00:16:49,871 --> 00:16:53,875
We'll open the bridge after all! This is our only chance!

268
00:16:55,627 --> 00:16:57,421
-All right! -It's all or nothing!

269
00:16:57,838 --> 00:16:59,631
Don't turn it on! Stop!

270
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:01,633
Hey! Don't touch it!

271
00:17:08,724 --> 00:17:10,058
The power's on!

272
00:17:10,267 --> 00:17:12,185
Okay! Turn on all the switches!

273
00:17:12,394 --> 00:17:13,228
Got it!

274
00:17:13,854 --> 00:17:15,480
Oh no! Stop all the cars now!

275
00:17:15,689 --> 00:17:16,565
Yes, sir.

276
00:17:16,773 --> 00:17:18,233
Stop! Open this door!

277
00:17:20,735 --> 00:17:23,488
Look! The signal at the Kachidoki Bridge is on!

278
00:17:23,697 --> 00:17:26,408
No way! That bridge isn't supposed to open anymore.

279
00:17:29,202 --> 00:17:32,664
Move your car! The bridge is opening!

280
00:17:39,796 --> 00:17:42,424
Please work, Kachidoki Bridge!

281
00:17:42,632 --> 00:17:44,050
Stop!

282
00:17:47,012 --> 00:17:47,971
Hey! Open up!

283
00:17:49,097 --> 00:17:51,475
Kachidoki Bridge, open!

284
00:18:13,413 --> 00:18:14,247
The bridge...

285
00:18:35,685 --> 00:18:38,647
Come on, open! Open more!

286
00:18:38,855 --> 00:18:40,232
Open wider!

287
00:18:44,903 --> 00:18:48,365
The bridge... It really does open.

288
00:18:58,083 --> 00:18:59,876
Ah! A police car...

289
00:19:02,087 --> 00:19:03,713
This is a disaster!

290
00:19:03,964 --> 00:19:05,840
Idiot! Lower the bridge right now!

291
00:19:13,265 --> 00:19:14,724
Open wider!

292
00:19:32,617 --> 00:19:34,744
All right! It's fully opened!

293
00:19:34,953 --> 00:19:36,413
We did it!

294
00:19:36,997 --> 00:19:38,415
The Kachidoki Bridge opened!

295
00:19:38,623 --> 00:19:40,417
Like it's raising its arms in victory.

296
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,919
The bridge opened again!

297
00:19:43,378 --> 00:19:46,590
That's how the Kachidoki Bridge is meant to be.

298
00:19:46,798 --> 00:19:49,259
It's the symbol of the Sumida River.

299
00:19:49,467 --> 00:19:50,927
This is really amazing!

300
00:19:53,013 --> 00:19:55,432
It's even better than I imagined, Kan-chan.

301
00:19:59,144 --> 00:20:00,645
Yeah, we did it!

302
00:20:01,563 --> 00:20:03,315
I hope Jun was watching.

303
00:20:11,072 --> 00:20:12,866
Hey! Open the door!

304
00:20:16,244 --> 00:20:19,414
Get ready, you guys! We'll arrest all of you!

305
00:20:19,623 --> 00:20:22,334
Oh, no! We can't get away. What should we do?

306
00:20:24,544 --> 00:20:25,378
Come with me!

307
00:20:26,171 --> 00:20:27,839
-What are you up to? -So long!

308
00:20:35,305 --> 00:20:38,099
Hey! Don't leave the bridge open!

309
00:20:39,225 --> 00:20:41,811
Damn it! What a bunch of idiots!

310
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:44,731
-Chief! -Help!

311
00:20:44,939 --> 00:20:46,983
Please help me!

312
00:20:58,286 --> 00:20:59,454
Let's get out of here!

313
00:21:02,957 --> 00:21:05,168
Hey, what's going on?

314
00:21:07,796 --> 00:21:11,925
Then, we swam to Hamarikyu, ran away, then came back

315
00:21:12,133 --> 00:21:16,221
to enjoy watching the big commotion at the Kachidoki Bridge.

316
00:21:16,972 --> 00:21:19,349
So you've always been a risk-taker.

317
00:21:19,557 --> 00:21:21,685
Jun-kun must have been so happy!

318
00:21:21,893 --> 00:21:25,730
Of course! I'll never forget his excited smile at that time!

319
00:21:26,147 --> 00:21:31,569
But why did he abandon his car and climb up the same bridge?

320
00:21:31,778 --> 00:21:33,446
He might have...

321
00:21:35,073 --> 00:21:36,449
He'd never do that.

322
00:21:36,658 --> 00:21:39,703
He had a weak body, but a strong mind.

323
00:21:39,911 --> 00:21:40,745
Excuse me.

324
00:21:42,706 --> 00:21:44,666
I'm the owner of the car outside.

325
00:21:44,874 --> 00:21:45,875
Jun!

326
00:21:48,545 --> 00:21:51,756
Kan-chan? Why are you here?

327
00:21:51,965 --> 00:21:54,009
Believe it or not, I'm a police officer.

328
00:21:54,217 --> 00:21:56,219
Kan-chan is a police officer?

329
00:21:57,262 --> 00:21:59,723
Don't laugh! You're the one illegally parked.

330
00:21:59,931 --> 00:22:05,186
Well, my car broke down, and I thought the mechanic would take it away for me.

331
00:22:05,395 --> 00:22:08,314
Oh, here's my card.

332
00:22:09,649 --> 00:22:13,445
A university professor? You've climbed the ladder, Jun!

333
00:22:13,653 --> 00:22:14,821
It's all thanks to you.

334
00:22:15,822 --> 00:22:20,702
I've never forgotten how you risked your life to open the bridge for me that day.

335
00:22:20,910 --> 00:22:22,829
Now I design bridges.

336
00:22:23,413 --> 00:22:26,708
Then, you were on the bridge because...

337
00:22:26,916 --> 00:22:29,210
There were some parts I wanted to look at.

338
00:22:29,419 --> 00:22:32,589
Yeah, that bridge is magnificent.

339
00:22:33,715 --> 00:22:36,801
Oh, Chief. This is my friend, a PhD in engineering...

340
00:22:37,427 --> 00:22:40,305
I heard everything, Ryotsu.

341
00:22:40,805 --> 00:22:42,891
Oh, were you listening?

342
00:22:43,099 --> 00:22:45,810
-The chief seems a bit off. -Yeah.

343
00:22:46,186 --> 00:22:51,107
You said when the bridge went up, a police officer was hanging onto it.

344
00:22:51,316 --> 00:22:57,947
That's right. It's so funny to remember. He kicked his legs in the air desperately,

345
00:22:58,156 --> 00:23:01,284
but ended up falling helplessly into the river with a big splash!

346
00:23:03,244 --> 00:23:06,414
And do you remember that officer's face?

347
00:23:07,165 --> 00:23:11,961
Of course! He had these nasty eyes, thick eyebrows,

348
00:23:12,170 --> 00:23:16,591
a long, droopy upper lip, and a mouth like a toad.

349
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:18,051
I can't forget...

350
00:23:18,259 --> 00:23:21,888
R-Ryo-chan, the face of the chief...

351
00:23:22,097 --> 00:23:23,556
The face of the chief?

352
00:23:23,932 --> 00:23:27,477
A toad-like mouth, a long upper lip, narrow eyes, thick eyebrows...

353
00:23:27,685 --> 00:23:28,812
N-No way...

354
00:23:35,527 --> 00:23:37,529
I am that police officer!

355
00:23:46,287 --> 00:23:50,291
Finally, I've met the idiot behind all that trouble.

356
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:53,002
Wait! Calm down, Chief!

357
00:23:54,420 --> 00:23:56,840
Get back here, Ryotsu!

358
00:23:57,048 --> 00:23:59,676
It was a long time ago!

359
00:24:04,514 --> 00:24:07,392
Yes! I won a ticket for a box seat at a sumo match!

360
00:24:07,642 --> 00:24:11,646
The box seat is for four people, so I'll invite Reiko and Nakagawa.

361
00:24:11,855 --> 00:24:13,815
Who should I take as the final person?

362
00:24:14,023 --> 00:24:18,153
Just kidding, Chief! I'll invite you too.

363
00:24:18,361 --> 00:24:20,321
NEXT EPISODE SUMO ALL THE WAY!

364
00:24:20,530 --> 00:24:23,074
Don't miss it!

365
00:24:32,959 --> 00:24:37,255
Let's keep smiling always

366
00:24:37,881 --> 00:24:41,509
Even when things go wrong

367
00:24:41,718 --> 00:24:45,972
Keep a pretty smile on your face

368
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:51,019
And go out as if nothing happened

369
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,106
Hey, show me your smile

370
00:24:55,315 --> 00:24:59,277
You did nothing wrong

371
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,781
Hey, show me your smile

372
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:07,410
Just like you did before, yeah

373
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
I want you to smile always

374
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:17,253
A woman with a frown isn't pretty

375
00:25:17,754 --> 00:25:23,301
So you should smile as soon as you can

376
00:25:24,093 --> 00:25:27,013
It's the grown-up thing to do

377
00:25:39,275 --> 00:25:44,072
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
